From c9f92b185f844929543850ce5b8e3a2a9fabd6aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix stock count DB provisioning and submit-line
 validation

- Dockerfile: switch startup command from `prisma migrate deploy` to
  `prisma db push` + seed. No migration was ever committed under
  backend/prisma/migrations, so `migrate deploy` was a silent no-op on
  every fresh `docker compose up --build`, leaving Postgres with zero
  tables and every API call failing with "relation does not exist".
- counts DTO: `SubmitCountLineDto.countedQty` had no class-validator
  decorator, so the global ValidationPipe (whitelist: true) silently
  stripped it from every request body. Submitting a counted quantity
  always persisted null, and the line stayed excluded from
  CountsService.complete()'s adjustment logic despite being marked
  COUNTED. Added @IsNumber/@Min(0).
- counts.service: stock count reference numbers were generated from a
  plain `count()+1`, which races under concurrent creates and can hit
  the unique constraint on `reference`. Added a bounded retry on P2002
  reference collisions instead of surfacing a 500.
- README: quick-start no longer needs the manual `migrate dev`/`seed`
  docker exec steps now that they run automatically on container start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
